1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,660
80 kilos.

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,120
32 kilometers per hour.

3
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:05,020
Just an 8% hill.

4
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:07,340
And your bike has no brakes!

5
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:08,300
Congratulations!

6
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,820
Holding that speed means

7
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:13,180
shedding about 560 watts.

8
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:15,060
Your shoes can't.

9
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:17,640
So you press a rubber pad on the rim.

10
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,240
That's a rim brake.

11
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:20,860
But you can't reach the

12
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:21,840
wheel while riding.

13
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:23,960
So a cable runs to a

14
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:25,100
lever on your handlebar.

15
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,000
Now squeezing stops you.

16
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:30,520
Then it rains and wet rims brake badly.

17
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:32,500
So you squeeze a disc on

18
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,080
the hub away from the rim.

19
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:35,680
That's a disc brake.

20
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:38,100
But cables stretch and drag.

21
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,480
So you swap the cable for fluid

22
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:42,660
in a sealed hose, like a syringe.

23
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,020
That's hydraulic.

24
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:45,640
On a long descent,

25
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,440
heat weakens the brakes.

26
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:49,420
So you fit a bigger rotor

27
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:50,940
which sheds heat better.

28
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:53,160
You built a modern disc brake.

29
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,200
It turns that hill into heat.

30
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:56,920
Your shoes can retire.

31
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:59,220
Save this for your next big hill.
